# compare.view: an arbitration, carried by the DECORATOR so the fallback is a
# native markdown table. The decorator hands the template ONE field, `rows`,
# so everything here lives in the rows: criteria as labels, and the verdict as
# a last row whose label the map below turns into a green chip.
#   @{view:compare}
#   | Criterion | Finding |
#   | --- | --- |
#   | speed   | option A wins, 3x |
#   | risk    | option B, A touches the parser |
#   | verdict | option A, the risk is bounded |
# The label column spends the tone slot, so `tone:` on the decorator restyles
# the whole board with no second file.
@tone key
@map labels verdict=success_bg
@fields rows label content
@box
@head {{box_title}}compare{{/}}
@each rows cap="1/4" bullet=""
 {{tone}}${label:labels}{{/}}  ${#bullet}${content}
@end
@endbox
